---
/*
  A7 - Prefill versus decode.
  Why one optimization helps prompt processing and not token generation.
  Prefill: a 512-token prompt becomes one large GEMM - every compute lane
  busy; the bottleneck is arithmetic, so a better kernel directly helps.
  Decode: one token at a time, the whole weight matrix streamed from DRAM per
  token - the memory bus saturates while compute lanes sit partly idle.
  The mechanism panel is schematic; the conclusion numbers are measured.
*/
import Fig from "../Fig.astro";
---

<Fig
  id="a7"
  title="A7 - Prefill versus decode"
  shows="Prompt processing is one big compute-bound GEMM - kernels matter. Decode streams the whole weight matrix from memory for every single token - bandwidth matters, kernels mostly cannot."
  data="schematic"
  dataNote="Mechanism panels are schematic. The conclusion is measured: moving Q3_K_L to Q4_0 on the CMF Phone 1 wins prompt +183% and loses decode -13% (docs/KLEIDIAI-QUANTS.md), because decode tracks bytes per weight, not kernel quality."
>
  <div id="a7-root" class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    <div class="rounded-[8px] border border-outline p-4">
      <p class="text-[0.75rem]"><span class="font-bold">PREFILL</span> <span class="text-dim">- 512 tokens, one large GEMM</span></p>
      <div class="mt-3 space-y-1.5" aria-hidden="true">
        {
          [0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => (
            <div class="h-3 rounded-[3px] bg-surface border border-outline overflow-hidden">
              <div class="a7-lane h-full w-full bg-fill" style={`animation-delay: ${i * 0.12}s`} />
            </div>
          ))
        }
        <p class="text-[0.6875rem] text-dim">compute lanes: all busy</p>
        <div class="h-2.5 rounded-[3px] bg-surface border border-outline overflow-hidden mt-2">
          <div class="a7-bus h-full w-1/3" style="background: var(--arm-2)"></div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[0.6875rem] text-dim">memory bus: comfortable</p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.75rem]">
        bottleneck: <span class="font-bold">arithmetic</span>
        <span class="text-dim">- a better kernel (KleidiAI, i8mm/SMMLA) directly helps</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-[8px] border border-outline p-4">
      <p class="text-[0.75rem]"><span class="font-bold">DECODE</span> <span class="text-dim">- one token at a time</span></p>
      <div class="mt-3 space-y-1.5" aria-hidden="true">
        {
          [0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => (
            <div class="h-3 rounded-[3px] bg-surface border border-outline overflow-hidden">
              <div
                class:list={["a7-lane-idle h-full", i < 2 ? "bg-fill w-2/5" : "w-1/5"]}
                style={i >= 2 ? "background: var(--arm-1)" : ""}
              />
            </div>
          ))
        }
        <p class="text-[0.6875rem] text-dim">compute lanes: waiting on data</p>
        <div class="h-2.5 rounded-[3px] border border-outline overflow-hidden mt-2 relative bg-surface">
          <div class="a7-busflow absolute inset-y-0 left-0 w-[200%]" style="background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, var(--warn) 0 10px, transparent 10px 16px)"></div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[0.6875rem]"><span class="t-warn">memory bus: saturated</span> <span class="text-dim">- the full weight matrix streams per token</span></p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.75rem]">
        bottleneck: <span class="font-bold">memory bandwidth</span>
        <span class="text-dim">- tracks bytes per weight; kernel quality cannot help a workload waiting on DRAM</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p slot="caption">
    This split is why the Q4_0 move wins prompt throughput by +183% and TTFT by -64% while decode
    gives up 13% (Q4_0 carries ~6% more bytes than Q3_K_L) - and why decode gains come from
    thread placement and count, not from kernels.
  </p>
</Fig>

<style>
  @keyframes a7pulse {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 0.55; }
    50% { opacity: 1; }
  }
  @keyframes a7flow {
    from { transform: translateX(-50%); }
    to { transform: translateX(0); }
  }
  [data-playing] .a7-lane {
    animation: a7pulse 1.2s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  [data-playing] .a7-busflow {
    animation: a7flow 1.1s linear infinite;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { registerFig, reducedMotion } from "../../scripts/figctl";

  const root = document.getElementById("a7-root");
  if (root && !reducedMotion()) {
    const fig = root.closest("[data-fig]") as HTMLElement;
    registerFig(fig, {
      start() {
        fig.setAttribute("data-playing", "");
      },
      pause() {
        fig.removeAttribute("data-playing");
      },
      resume() {
        fig.setAttribute("data-playing", "");
      },
      replay() {
        fig.setAttribute("data-playing", "");
      },
    });
  }
</script>
